# A dataset with RDF-star QUOTED TRIPLES in it — the shape that was, until the
# writers learned the RDF 1.2 surface, unpublishable.
#
# rete stores a quoted triple as `<<s p o>>`, and the exporter used to emit that
# verbatim. `oxigraph convert --from-format nq` REJECTS it ("The object of a
# triple must be an IRI, a blank node or a literal"), so the driver's required
# parse check would have refused this dump in every spelling — recorded as a
# latent limitation in #257 because none of the 11 swept datasets had one. This
# fixture is what stops that from being latent: it goes through the real
# exporter, the real gate and the real referee, and it must come out `done`.
#
# Everything here is in OBJECT position, which is where RDF 1.2 puts a triple
# term (`ttSubject ::= iri | BlankNode`). A subject-position quoted triple has
# no RDF 1.2 spelling at all and the exporter refuses it by name; that case is
# covered by `cargo test -p rete-cli --test export_quoted_triples`, not here,
# because this harness is about what DOES get published.
#
# Nesting, a typed literal inside the quoted triple, and a blank node on both
# sides — the shapes a writer that split on spaces or counted angle brackets
# would corrupt.
<http://example.org/occ1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/BarnSwallow> .
<http://example.org/jsmith> <http://example.org/recorded> << <http://example.org/occ1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/BarnSwallow> >> .
<http://example.org/claim1> <http://example.org/states> << <http://example.org/occ1> <http://example.org/individualCount> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> >> .
<http://example.org/claim2> <http://example.org/states> << <http://example.org/occ1> <http://example.org/observedOn> "2023-05-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> >> .
<http://example.org/meta> <http://example.org/about> << <http://example.org/jsmith> <http://example.org/recorded> << <http://example.org/occ1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/BarnSwallow> >> >> .
_:src <http://example.org/attests> << _:obs <http://example.org/label> "a > b, and a << inside"@en >> .
